# Slaughterhouse Poultry Brine, Injection, and Spritz

Source: [Smoked-Meat.com Forum — Tip Piper, Hillbilly Vittles](https://www.smoked-meat.com/forum/forum/poultry/186-slaughterhouse-poultry-brine-injection-spritz)

## Recipe Name: Slaughterhouse Poultry Brine, Injection, and Spritz

## Servings: Enough for 1 whole chicken or turkey

## Prep Time: 15 mins

## Cook Time: N/A (brine, injection, and spritz only)

## Ingredients:
### Brine:
- 1.5 gal water
- 1/2 cup salt (pickling or kosher)
- 1/2 cup dark brown sugar
- 2 tsp garlic powder
- 2 tsp onion powder
- 2 tsp Cajun seasoning
- 2 tsp celery seed

### Injection:
- 1/2 packet Good Seasons Italian dressing mix
- 2 tsp garlic powder
- 2 tsp celery seed
- 2 tbsp unsalted butter, melted
- 2 cups apple cider

### Spritz (good for everything):
- 8 oz apple cider
- 6 oz water
- 4 oz whiskey
- 2 oz cider vinegar

## Instructions:
1. **Brine:** Combine water, salt, brown sugar, garlic powder, onion powder, Cajun seasoning, and celery seed. Stir until salt and sugar dissolve. Submerge poultry and refrigerate to brine.
2. **Injection:** Whisk together dressing mix, garlic powder, celery seed, melted butter, and apple cider until well combined. Load into a meat injector and inject throughout the bird before cooking.
3. **Spritz:** Combine apple cider, water, whiskey, and cider vinegar in a spray bottle. Spritz the poultry periodically during smoking/cooking to keep the surface moist.

## Notes:
- Recipe as posted; untested by me — adjust seasoning/sweetness to taste.
- Spritz works well on other smoked meats too, not just poultry.

